`quarto install chrome-headless-shell` (and `quarto install chromium`, which redirects to it) fails on Linux arm64 with HTTP 404.

The scheduled `Test Tool Install` workflow run failed on both `ubuntu-24.04-arm` jobs (`Install tools` and `Chromium deprecation redirect`) with a 404 downloading the arm64 zip:

https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/actions/runs/34106144146

`playwrightCdnDownloadUrl()` builds the download URL from Playwright's old CDN layout, keyed by revision:

https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/blob/136d0838d1bb80baca2c7923525f55f7db64a969/src/tools/impl/chrome-for-testing.ts#L194-L200

That resolves to `https://cdn.playwright.dev/builds/chromium/{revision}/chromium-headless-shell-linux-arm64.zip`, which 404s. Playwright's own registry moved to a `browserVersion`-keyed path with a `chrome-` prefix instead of `chromium-`:

[source](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/312030cdcee20c006343e5f8420fe451b9aa6390/packages/playwright-core/src/server/registry/index.ts#L117-L126)
```ts
function cftUrl(suffix: string): DownloadPathFunction {
  return ({ browserVersion }) => {
    return {
      path: `builds/cft/${browserVersion}/${suffix}`,
      mirrors: [
        'https://cdn.playwright.dev',
      ],
    };
  };
}
```
used for `chrome-headless-shell` on linux arm64 as `cftUrl('linux-arm64/chrome-headless-shell-linux-arm64.zip')`.

I confirmed the old URL 404s and the new pattern (`https://cdn.playwright.dev/builds/cft/{browserVersion}/linux-arm64/chrome-headless-shell-linux-arm64.zip`) redirects to `storage.googleapis.com/chrome-for-testing-public`. CfT's own `last-known-good-versions-with-downloads.json` still doesn't list `linux-arm64` downloads for `chrome-headless-shell` (only `mac-arm64`), so the Playwright CDN fallback from #11877 is still needed, only the URL template is stale.

This affects the currently supported v1.10 release too, so I'll backport the fix.

